{"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Flows","roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"OnboardingKit"}]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Features","anchor":"Features","identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/Pages-Article","doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/Screens-Article","doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/USPs-Article","doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/WhatsNew-Article","doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/Views-Article"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/onboardingkit\/flows-article"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"OnboardingKit has flows that can present multiple pages, like ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingPageFlow","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingSlideshow","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Both use the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingPageState","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" described in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/Pages-Article","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and can render any page models and views you want.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Page-Flow","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Page Flow"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingPageFlow","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" presents pages that the user navigates manually, with swipes, arrow keys, and edge taps. It shows a page indicator below the pages.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"numberOfColumns":5,"columns":[{"size":2,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"OnboardingPageFlow"}]}]},{"size":3,"content":[{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["OnboardingPageFlow(","    state: state,","    content: { page in","        OnboardingPageContent {","            Text(\"Page \\(page.pageIndex + 1)\")","        }","    },","    bottomButtons: { state in","        OnboardingButton(state.isLastPage ? \"Done\" : \"Next\") {","            withAnimation {","                state.showNextPage(orDismiss: dismiss)","            }","        }","    }",")",".onboardingPageFlowStyle(...)"]}]}],"type":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The view can be styled with an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingPageFlowStyle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which can be applied with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingPageFlowStyle(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". It defines the page indicator colors, as well as how page content fades out above the page indicator.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Apply ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingPageFlowContentFade()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to scrolling page content, to fade it out before it reaches the indicators. Screens like ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWelcomeScreen","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWhatsNewScreen","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" already do this.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Slideshow","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Slideshow"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingSlideshow","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" presents pages that automatically progress after a certain duration, like a story. It shows a progress bar for each page at the top of the view, and calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"onStoryCompleted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the last page has been presented.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"numberOfColumns":5,"columns":[{"size":2,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"OnboardingSlideshow","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"size":3,"content":[{"code":["OnboardingSlideshow(","    state: state,","    onStoryCompleted: { dismiss() },","    content: { page in","        OnboardingPageContent {","            Text(\"Slide \\(page.pageIndex + 1)\")","        }","    },","    bottomButtons: { state in","        OnboardingButton(state.isLastPage ? \"Done\" : \"Next\") {","            withAnimation {","                state.showNextPage(orDismiss: dismiss)","            }","        }","    }",")",".onboardingSlideshowStyle(...)",".onboardingSlideshowConfiguration(...)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"type":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The user can tap the top progress bars to jump to a certain page. On iOS and visionOS, the user can also tap the left and right side of a slide to move back and forth, and long press to pause the slideshow.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The view can be styled with an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingSlideshowStyle","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which can be applied with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingSlideshowStyle(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". It defines the colors and height of the progress bars, which are rendered with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingSlideshowProgressView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A slideshow can be configured with an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingSlideshowConfiguration","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", which is applied with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingSlideshowConfiguration(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". It defines the slide duration, the progress timer tick increment, and the accessibility labels of the tap areas.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Bottom-Buttons","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Bottom Buttons"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Both flows have an optional ","type":"text"},{"code":"bottomButtons","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" builder, which can be used to add buttons like ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingButton","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to the bottom of the flow. The builder is called with the page state, to let you navigate between pages and adapt the buttons to the page.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"This article describes the OnboardingKit flows, like page flows and slideshows.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/Flows-Article","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Topics","identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingPageF